  "_comment": "Demo state only. The two prepared states of the demo switch and their sample records. Every record here is a sample: it is marked as one on screen, never mixed with a traveler's own records, never sent to an account and never read outside the demo state. Dates are relative (daysAgo + local time) so the trip always ends today. Savings are computed by the app's rules, not stored: haggles from asked and paid, ATM results from the screen figures with the same rule as the ATM scan. Receipt figures must add up (checked when the file is read) or the file is refused. The visitor's trip is a 4-day first visit to Bangkok given by the project owner (Day 1: Suvarnabhumi arrival, exchange, taxi to Asok, Terminal 21, hotel; Day 2: ICONSIAM, Asiatique, Chao Phraya boat, Khao San Road; Day 3: Wat Arun, Siam Paragon, Chatuchak; Day 4, today: breakfast, cafe, ATM, then lunch and the 23:00 flight). Prices are realistic 2026 Bangkok amounts chosen for the demo (exchange rates around 31-32 THB per USD, ATM fee 220 THB); street prices sit inside the usual ranges of market_prices.json, whose sources are listed there (see NOTES.md). Coordinates are OpenStreetMap positions of each place. Each persona's 'calendar' holds sample events for today (time, title, a place Google Maps can find) for the morning briefing; they are samples too and only read in the demo state. Cash: each sample says how it was paid ('paidWith': cash or card). The sample cash balance is computed from these records by the same ledger rules as a traveler's own (ATM withdrawal adds the amount taken out, cash-paid haggles and receipts subtract what was paid, card payments leave cash alone); 'cashMovements' lists only cash activity that has no record of its own, such as a currency exchange, a taxi or a deposit, and the balance never goes below zero. Each persona's 'trip' gives its trip dates relative to today (first day startDaysAgo, last day endDaysAhead), shown as 'Day n of m'; its sample calendar only has events today.",
